sonant (Gram.); ‘sounding’. Of the explosive sounds (see above). some (b, d, g) are accompanied by vibration of the vocal cords & are called voiced or sonant; others (p, k, t) are without such vibration & are called unvoiced, voiceless, mute, or surd;
===
*sonant* (Gram.); 'sounding'. Of the *explosive* sounds (see above). some (b, d, g) are accompanied by vibration of the vocal cords & are called *voiced* or *sonant*; others (p, k, t) are without such vibration & are called *unvoiced*, *voiceless*, *mute*, or *surd*;
>>>
<<<
 when whispered, the sonants are not clearly distinguishable from the corresponding surds. See also voiced below.
===
 when whispered, the sonants are not clearly distinguishable from the corresponding surds. See also *voiced* below.
